# Purpose
Provide a copyable, self-contained design example for Wide opening, Phone
portrait, Compact Fold and Adaptive focus layouts. Local controls demonstrate
moving the same useful cells to match Work, Verify and Deliver priorities.

# Dependencies
- ../how-to/build-agent-iq-metal-layouts.md documents usage and limits.
- No external libraries, fonts, resources, network or dashboard APIs.

# Gotchas
- Every scenario is labelled illustrative. Nothing claims real work completion.
- Scenario controls/functions are local example code, not a GreatVibe API.
- The optional script region can be copied into a capable Agent IQ runtime;
  the outer document is a standalone preview wrapper, not a tool payload.
- Responsive rules use available region width and height. Preserve viewer
  allocation and reduced motion; never force parent size or scroll position.
- Prefer the canonical greatVibe symbol without a duplicate wordmark.
- Canonical path opacity and rounded caps use inline style so script-region
  preparation preserves them as well as direct standalone browser rendering.
- The copyable region owns its html/body size and padding reset. Its size
  container must retain a definite height inside the isolated runtime, whose
  default body padding would otherwise collapse full-height composition.
- Short phone allocations condense to a small core and the current useful cell;
  supporting cells yield before the stage/focus/next labels. No document height
  floor may exceed the viewer allocation. Short Fold retains three cell titles.
- Preview controls use an allowlisted DIV with role=group; unsupported NAV
  wrappers are unwrapped during script preparation and would break grid rows.

# Change History
- 2026-09-20: Added the network-free responsive example and accessible controls.
